---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, SITE_NAMES } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Cookies on ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: Clarity analytics and opt-out`} description="The sales tax and property tax calculators set no cookie of their own. The site measures page use with Microsoft Clarity: its cookies, lifetimes and how to opt out at any time." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookies' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>Cookies</h1>
    <p>The sales tax, reverse sales tax and property tax calculators set no cookie of their own, and the site shows no advertising.</p>
    <h2>Analytics: Microsoft Clarity</h2><p>The site loads Microsoft Clarity, operated by Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, to see which state pages are read and where visitors stop. A notice on your first visit says so and offers an opt-out. Clarity keeps anonymous session recordings and heatmaps of clicks and scrolling; prices, local rates and home values you type are masked in the browser before anything is sent. Cookies: <code>_clck</code> (one year) and <code>_clsk</code> (one day), plus <code>MUID</code> and <code>CLID</code> that Microsoft may set on its own domains.</p>
    <h2>Opting out</h2><p>Click “Opt out” in the notice, or later “Cookie settings” in the footer, and Clarity stops loading. Your answer is stored in <code>localStorage</code> as <code>consent-choice</code> and never leaves your browser. Clearing this site’s data deletes cookies already set; blocking third-party cookies or the clarity.ms domain also works.</p>
    <p>More in the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a>. Questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
